Falsifies `inter_process_communication::timer::verification::the_cache_is_never_later_than_an_armed_deadline`.

The defect: arming overwrites the cache with the new deadline instead of taking the minimum. It
reads naturally, because "the next thing due" is what was just armed, and it is right whenever only
one timer is armed, which is every single-consumer test.

Expected to fail: `cache_is_sound` after an arm, whenever another timer was already armed earlier
than the new deadline: that timer's expiry is now invisible to the tick.

diff --git a/crates/inter_process_communication/src/timer.rs b/crates/inter_process_communication/src/timer.rs
index 5e38c9a0c..5ceab0715 100644
--- a/crates/inter_process_communication/src/timer.rs
+++ b/crates/inter_process_communication/src/timer.rs
@@ -137,7 +137,7 @@ impl<T: Copy> Timer<T> {
 /// **The cache after arming `deadline`**: never raised, only lowered. Called under the same lock
 /// as the arm, so the cache and the timers never disagree for anyone who holds it.
 pub fn lowered(cached: u64, deadline: u64) -> u64 {
-    cached.min(deadline)
+    deadline
 }
 
 /// **Whether the tick must walk.** The one comparison per idle tick `notes/timed-wait.md` priced.
